 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Current gain grades",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Gain at IC = -200 mA and VCE = -5.0 V is binned into three ranks: R covers 60 to 120, O 100 to 200 and Y 160 to 320. The rank is the last character of the four-character marking on the body (1013R, 1013O, 1013Y)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "At VCE = -5 V the gain stays between about 140 and 280 from -1 mA to about -400 mA, higher at 100 °C than at 25 °C, then falls steeply towards -1 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With the base driven at one tenth of the collector current, VCE(sat) is about -30 mV up to -20 mA and rises to roughly -310 to -360 mV at -1 A, a little higher at 100 °C than at -25 °C (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about -440 to -580 mV at -1 mA to about -890 to -950 mV at -1 A, lower in magnitude at 100 °C (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Measured at 1 MHz, input capacitance Cib falls from about 260 pF at -0.1 V reverse bias to about 130 pF at -6 V, and output capacitance Cob from about 64 pF at -0.1 V to about 13 pF at -20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-89 body uses a molding compound rated UL 94V-0, is RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, with lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C."
  }
 ],
